mindmap
root((how a model learns to use this plugin))
  four orders of magnitude, and only two of them are free
    the catalog: 3381 characters, always visible
      7 rows, the longest at 498 of 500
        a row past 500 loses its tail to the model, silently
    the tool descriptions: 30357 characters, always visible
      14 descriptions, the longest at 3382 characters
        no ceiling here, so a description grows without anything objecting
    a skill body: the bodies together are 78839 characters, loaded one at a time
      the model chooses it from the row alone
    the references: 177052 characters, on follow-through
      the only part paid for by need rather than by default
  what the always-visible text has to carry
    the words a user would say
      matching is literal, so the phrasing decides
        read a report reaches the row, reading one does not
    the sibling that owns the adjacent case
      a row that names none leaves the model choosing between look-alikes
    the non-goal, beside the scope claim
      without it the neighbouring job gets done here, confidently and wrongly
    and nothing else
      the budget is why: space spent on praise is space not spent on a trigger
  where each property stands today
    skill rows: 7 of 7 name a sibling, 7 of 7 state a non-goal
    tool descriptions: 14 of 14 name a sibling, 14 of 14 state a non-goal
      the ones that name none: 
    and the result routes onward in 6 of 6 families
      that is the only channel that can redirect a model mid-task
  what each tool owns, and where the case beside it goes
    model_automaton_verify: a finite-word language, and its relation to another automaton
      not this: the question is reachability or deadlock inside one state machine - that is model_verify
    model_compose_verify: several machines run together: rendezvous, shared locations, lost updates
      not this: the question is about one machine on its own - that is model_verify
    model_interleaving_scan: mining a document or plan for concurrency claims, and routing each to the analysis that decides it
      not this: the protocol itself has to be decided - that is model_compose_verify
    model_datamodel_verify: entities, keys, migrations, and whether the data survived them
      not this: the question is about behaviour over time rather than stored state - that is model_verify
    model_design_review: a design's own declarations: layering, responsibility, substitutability, interface width
      not this: the question is a fact about the graph - does this edge exist - that is uml_structure_verify
    model_edit: one editing round on a model file, answered with the structural diff and the change in findings
      not this: the edit is done and the model has to be decided again - that is model_verify
    model_export: a model translated into UPPAAL, TLA+, PRISM or SPIN for a property this plugin does not decide
      not this: the property can be decided here - that is model_verify
    report_diff: what changed between two reports of the same family
      not this: the current report does not exist yet - that is model_verify
    uml_structure_verify: a dependency graph as a graph - cycles, layers, dangling edges - from a drawing or a source tree
      not this: the question is a rule the design declared for itself, not an edge that exists - that is model_design_review
    uml_explain_labels: the label spellings a notation accepts and the directives that pin the rest
      not this: a diagram has to be read rather than explained - that is uml_parse
    uml_parse: reading a diagram back into the model its family declares
      not this: the question is whether the diagram says something sound - that is uml_review
    uml_render: drawing a model in the notation that can carry its family
      not this: the question is whether the modelling is sound - that is uml_review
    uml_review: auditing the modelling: reachability, ambiguity, round-trip fidelity, family-specific defects
      not this: the claim is about behaviour rather than the drawing - that is model_verify
    model_verify: one machine: reachable states, invariants, deadlock, and a before/after regression
      not this: two or more machines must handshake or share a location - that is model_compose_verify
  the five routes that do not need luck
    a rejection names the tool that would accept the input
      the model is already holding the wrong one when it finds out
    nextSteps names a tool, not an idea
    a finding code carries its domain in the prefix
    the report states which schema it follows
    a description names its neighbour and its edge
  what each description decides, and what it costs to have it
    a description earns its space three ways: what it decides, when that pays, what to use instead
    model_automaton_verify - 0 tokens, instead: model_verify, model_compose_verify
    model_compose_verify - 0 tokens, instead: model_verify
    model_interleaving_scan - 0 tokens, instead: model_verify, model_compose_verify
    model_datamodel_verify - 0 tokens, instead: model_verify, uml_structure_verify
    model_design_review - 0 tokens, instead: uml_structure_verify
    model_edit - 0 tokens, instead: model_datamodel_verify, model_design_review, model_verify
    model_export - 0 tokens, instead: model_verify
    report_diff - 0 tokens, instead: model_verify, model_datamodel_verify, model_design_review, uml_review, uml_structure_verify, model_interleaving_scan
    uml_structure_verify - 0 tokens, instead: model_design_review, model_verify
    uml_explain_labels - 0 tokens, instead: uml_parse, uml_review
    uml_parse - 0 tokens, instead: uml_review
    uml_render - 0 tokens, instead: uml_review, uml_parse
    uml_review - 0 tokens, instead: model_verify
    model_verify - 0 tokens, instead: model_compose_verify
    every description states its boundary
  why a map rather than a paragraph
    the budget is spatial, so the picture has to be spatial
      a row is a fixed width, and every sentence competes for it
    the reader is deciding what to add and where
      the answer differs by surface, so the surfaces are the branches
    and the numbers move
      a generated map is re-measured; a remembered one is wrong within a release
  what this map does not claim
    not that any input routes correctly
      the corpus measures constructed boundaries, not a distribution
    not that the tool surface has been measured at all
      there is no corpus of tool-selection cases yet
    not that a longer description is better
      it is only unbounded, which makes it the easiest surface to waste
